Z||000031||artherd||09-04-2001||11:44 PM||||If you are not willing to drive an S2000 in *ONLY* the range that would cause a fiero's engine to explode, it will be slow.<P>Here's why.<BR> <A HREF="http://s2000.vtec.net/dyno/dyno1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://s2000.vtec.net/dyno/dyno1.html</A> <P>(keep in mind numbers are rw.)<P>Yes, VTEC is a clever way of essentially cramming two seperate cams in an engine, one for low-end, and one for high.<P>You *could* use just the high-lobe cam in your engine, but then it would *really* make no torque  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  (so that's why I say the VTEC cams are a low-end booster for sissies who don't flog the crap out of their cars all teh time*)<P>*== kidding :S)<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000032||Turbo88||09-04-2001||11:48 PM||||Well I disagree. They are not much nicer cars. I've driven them. Buy an Audi TT or a Mercedes C230. Lets see, My Fiero has won both SCCA events it has competed in. Hmmm, It has a 13 second time slip.. I guess I would be asking too much to believe that someone had an S2000 in one of the classes I ran in? <P>But I guess you can get me on one thing, The engine is out of it right now for A new cam and valvetrain. But I have both SCCA awards and a time slip if you would like me to scan it for you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. <P>Honestly, it's all opinion. And don't get me wrong, the drive train in those cars it damn cool! The handle decently well and are quite peppy. Over look the cool factor of the 9k engine (not very streetable as I recall driving it). All I can say is if you like them, then sell your fiero and buy one. I will catch ya on the street sometime <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">..||||reg||1
Z||000033||Turbo88||09-05-2001||10:14 AM||||               <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by TRiAD:<BR><B> <A HREF="http://maps.yahoo.com/py/maps.py?BFCat=&Pyt=Tmap&newFL=Use+Address+Below&addr=&csz=Creve+Coeur%2C+IL&country=us&Get%A0Map=Get+Map" TARGET=_blank>http://maps.yahoo.com/py/maps.py?BFCat=&Pyt=T               map&newFL=Use+Address+Below&addr=&csz=Creve+Coeur%2C+IL&country=us&Get%A0Map=Get+Map</A> <P><BR>sheesh. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What is the sheesh for? I just said I thought it was a small world. Is that ok?<BR> [URL=http://maps.yahoo.com/py/maps.py?Pyt=Tmap&addr=&city=Creve+Coeur&state=MO&slt=38.660800&sln=-90.422500&name=&zip=&country=us&BFKey=&BFCat=&BFClient=&mag=8&desc=&cs=7&newmag=7&  poiti]http://maps.yahoo.com/py/maps.py?Pyt=Tmap&addr=&city=Creve+Coeur&state=MO&slt=38.660800&sln=-90.422500&name=&zip=&country=us&BFKey=&BFCat=&BFClient=&mag=8&desc=&cs=7&newmag=7 &poititle=&poi=[/URL]  <P>sheesh<P><p>[This message has been edited by Turbo88 (edited 09-05-2001).]||||reg||1
